    "Mackenzie and I wash up as quick as we can before pulling into my truck, and I drive her down to the sheriff’s office."

    "When I turn the corner towards my usual parking spot, I find it blocked off by a huge pick-up truck, much newer than mine."

    mcmac "I’m going to take a guess and say that’s Beau’s."

    ma "Especially with those Wisconsin plates."

    "We enter the office together, and a tall man is waiting right inside the door."

    "His presence fills the entire room, and my heart beats faster when he looks at me."

    "It’s a primal response, a hundred red flags in my head telling me to run. Then Mackenzie steps in front of me, cutting off his gaze."

    ma "You must be Beau Rider."

    beau "And you must be Sheriff Hunt."
    beau "I hear one of my boys was raising a bit of a ruckus over here."

    "(A ruckus? Damien was trying to take Mackenzie’s territory to impress him.)"

    ma "That’s a kind way to summarise kidnapping, repeated assaults and property damage."

    beau "Kidnapping? Who did he take?"

    "Mackenzie’s eyes narrow, and she gestures over to her desk."

    "Beau moves to follow, and I stay right behind Mackenzie as she settles in her seat."

    ma "A local girl."

    "Beau raises a brow before looking over to Mackenzie’s deputy."

    "He’s quietly rocking out on his headphones, oblivious to what’s happening across the room."

    beau "He get his teeth in her?"

    ma "No."

    beau "Then it’s just a misunderstanding."
    beau "I’ll pay his bail and we’ll get things settled."

    "He smiles, wide enough that I feel a twist in my gut."

    "It’s the good-ol’-boy look I’ve seen from too many men, writing off someone else’s pain like something they picked out of their teeth."

    "Mackenzie must feel it too."

    "The drawer she yanks open squeals in protest before she takes out a stack of papers and a scan of Damien’s ID."

    ma "The money’s meaningless."

    beau "Think of it as a donation to the town for their...upset."
    beau "You know our kind didn’t keep well behind bars, Sheriff. It’s not how we do things."

    mcmac "How do you do things?"

    "Beau frowns, as if surprised I dared to speak, and I catch him sniffing the air."

    "His eyes flicker between Mackenzie and I for a moment before her lets out a low laugh."

    beau "Why don’t you ask her about that, Miss...?"

    mcmac "[genericfn]. You can drop the Miss."

    beau "I think I just felt my mother turn over in her grave."

    beau "But regardless, [genericfn], I think you ought to keep to your place."

    "I hear something crack."

    "When I look down, the pen in Mackenzie’s hand is broken,"

    "and from the tremble in her arm, I think she’s fighting not to shift and get right in Beau’s face."

    "(He’s an asshole, but I need to calm things down.)"

