    "Mackenzie gets another open, signing a messy signature at the bottom before handing the papers to Beau."

    ma "Cash or credit?"

    beau "Cash, of course."

    "He pulls out a roll of hundred dollar bills, counting out a stack into the thousands before dropping it on Mackenzie’s desk."

    beau "I’m sure that will cover your repairs."

    "She doesn’t answer him, standing up and walking over to the cell in the back."

    "Damien stands up when Mackenzie fits her keys into the lock, only to back up against the wall when Beau comes into view."

    beau "You seem to have bitten off more than you can chew, Damien."

    dam "Yes, sir."

    beau "We’re going to have a talk about that. A long one."

    "Damien swallows hard, and even when Mackenzie pulls the door open, it takes him a minute to pull himself together and walk out of the cell."

    "(Annabelle was scared earlier, but Damien looks like he just caught an express to hell.)"

    "(I can’t believe I feel a little bad for this guy.)"

    "He nods and darts past Mackenzie, not even looking back."

    "The deputy sits up at the sound of the door slamming shut, tugging out his headphones."

