    sid1 "Everything okay, Sheriff?"

    ma "Yeah, Elmer. Keep writing up reports."
    ma "Mr. Rider and I need to have a private chat outside."

    "Elmer shrugs and returns to his music, divers flying across his keyboard in endless clicks."

    "Beau levels Mackenzie with a look, openly sizing her up."

    beau "You sure about this, Hunt?"

    ma "Yes. Yes, I am."

    beau "Then let’s take a little stroll."

    "Beau leaves the station first, but after Mackenzie and I get through the door, she stops me by grabbing my elbow."

    ma "I need you to go to the bowling alley and stay there."
    ma "Razi and JD will look out for you."

    mcmac "I’m not leaving you alone with that guy. He’s bad news."

    "She sighs, fingers relaxing."

    ma "He can also hear you."

    "I gulp, looking back over my shoulder. Beau is on the opposite side of the street, but from his smile, I know he’s taken in every word."

    beau "Come on, Sheriff. You can bring your partner."
    beau "She clearly made of stern stuff if she runs with you."

    "(That’s why he was checking my scent. Great.)"

    "Mackenzie’s obvious reluctance sparks even more tension between the two of them, and I take her hand, leaning over to whisper in her ear."

    mcmac "I’ll be okay. I promise."

    ma "Don’t fall out of my sight."

    "I nod, and she relaxes a little, rubbing her thumb along the back of my knuckles. Beau gets into his car, and I hand Mackenzie my keys."

    mcmac "Want to drive?"

    ma "Yes, thank you."

    "We follow Beau all the way to the outskirts of the town, where the road turns into a stretch of dirt framed by fields."

    "When he gets out of his truck, Damien doesn’t come with him."

    ma "Exile or execution."

    mcmac "What?"

    ma "That’s what happens to werewolves that break territorial rules. We can’t stay in human prisons."
    ma "So those are the alternatives."

    mcmac "Is Damien getting exiled?"

    ma "That depends if Beau thinks he’s still useful. But his odds aren’t great."

    "(Oh boy. This is going to be rough.)"

    "I give Mackenzie’s hand one last squeeze before we get out of the car together."

    "Beau looks far too relaxed as she approaches, casually adjusting the brim of his hat."

    beau "Mackenzie Hunt. I heard the wolf finally came back to your family, but I wasn’t expecting you to be an alpha too."

    beau "I bet your parents are proud."

    "Mackenzie’s jaw tightens a degree before all the emotion drains from her face."

    "(Her parents still don’t know.)"

    ma "Stay out of my territory, Rider. You and anyone bearing your name."
    ma "You sent Damien here to claim land that wasn’t his."

    beau "Hold on now. He did that on his own accord."
    beau "You tell a man to prove himself and sometimes he makes mistakes. I’ll make sure Damien’s held accountable for it."

    ma "I’m not overseeing his punishment. I care that the boundaries are respected."

    beau "Of course."
    beau "I’ll keep an eye on my pack, Hunt. Although I’d love to meet yours."

    "He extends his arm for a handshake, but when Mackenzie moves to return it, they grasp each other’s forearms tight."

    "Beau lets out a growl that rolls from between his teeth like thunder, holding her gaze and refusing to back down."

    "I stare in shock as Mackenzie starts to shift, eyes bleeding to bright gold and sharp teeth suddenly bared."

    "Beau doesn’t let go of her, even though claws are now cutting into his sleeve."
