    ma "This is my town, and now it’s my state."

    beau "It’s a big responsibility."

    ma "You think I don’t know that?"

    beau "I guess we’ll see."

    "Beau’s hand relaxes first, and once Mackenzie lets go, he casually smoothes out the wrinkles in his sleeve."

    "I watch as he gets back into his truck, with Damien sitting dejected in the passenger seat."

    "Mackenzie watches the car until it disappears completely out of view."

    "(That was...a lot.)"

    mcmac "Did Beau hurt you?"

    ma "No, he didn’t hurt me."
    ma "He forced me to shift. It was a show of power."

    "I flash back to Mackenzie interrogating Annabelle back at the station, the moment their eyes turned gold and she buckled under the questions."

    "(I didn’t realise alpha could do it to each other. But if Beau is a old as he says...)"

    mcmac "Was that true?"

    ma "Was what true?"

    mcmac "He said he knew your great-grandparents. That would make him super old."

    ma "I don’t know if Beau knew them as well as he implied, but yeah, he’s that old."

    "I do the math one more time, even counting on my fingers for good measure."

    "(No wonder Mackenzie isn’t bothered by Diego’s age.)"

    mcmac "Could...could you live that long?"

    ma "Potentially. But we’re not immortal."
    ma "Enough damage or enough silver, even someone like Beau won’t survive."
    ma "Speaking of..."

    "Mackenzie reaches into her back pocket and pulls out Damien’s knife."

    "It’s folded shut, but I can still see the shine on the smooth edge of the blade."

    mcmac "You kept it?"

    ma "I sure didn’t want him trying to use it again. But I don’t need it."
    ma "You do."

    "I immediately hesitate, knowing how much it could hurt her."

    "Even by accident, I don’t want a weapon like that near Mackenzie."

    mcmac "We could just get rid of the knife."

    ma "In the last two hours, we’ve had a pair of werewolves show up that I didn’t expect."
    ma "Beau was right about one thing. If any pack shows up, I am outnumbered."
    ma "And I don’t want you getting hurt because of that."

    "She presses the knife into my hand, and I turn it over, trying to get used to its weight."

    mcmac "Are you sure?"

    ma "It’s okay, [genericfn]. Just a precaution."

    mcmac "Alright."

    "I shove it deep into my pocket, wanting to make sure no part of the blade sticks out."

    "Mackenzie’s ears twitch a little when it goes out of view, and the tension shows in the taut lines of her forearms."

    mcmac "Are you going to change back?"

    ma "Not yet. I..."
    ma "Usually I can shake off my instincts, but they’re biting at me something fierce after seeing Beau."
    ma "I’ll feel better if I get a lay of the land, make sure no one is here that shouldn’t be."

    "(I can’t run around at her speed, but we could always take the car.)"

